WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.340
SPEAKER: With almost 500
sessions at Next 2018,

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.590
it's understandable that you
couldn't get to them all.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.750
So if you didn't see "Google's
Vision for a Safer Web,"

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.500
then stay tuned because
here's the rewind.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.753
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.660
Over the past year,
we've seen amazing growth

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.880
from large and small
companies who are embracing

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.260
the web for productivity.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.430
This means coworkers
are relying on the web

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.580
more and more for things
like collaboration,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.830
remote working, and the
cloud-based services that

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.870
help them accomplish
their goals each day.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.110
Sadly, attackers are
following this trend as well

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.610
and getting more creative.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.170
We've seen more
attacks each year

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:38.720
and more variety in
the kinds of attacks.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.220
Completely new attacks
are appearing as well.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.970
Most of these attempt to gain
control of high-value accounts

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.340
so the attacker can use the
credentials for their own

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.640
purposes, which means
that the defense--

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.190
that's probably you--
needs new strategies too.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.780
And Google is here to help.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.420
We've been rolling out more
tools and features to Chrome

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.490
to help secure your
company's resources

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.020
and keep your employees safe.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.510
At Google, we're very familiar
with these kinds of attacks.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.900
We see over 6,000 instances
of unwanted software attacks

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.930
each minute, targeting
over 3 billion devices

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.010
around the world.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.690
And thanks to our
Safe Browsing tools,

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.700
we can learn from these
attacks and recognize

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.190
new vulnerabilities
automatically.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.420
And here's the best part--

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.570
your IT administrator can
get access to the same tools

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:23.090
and capabilities
through Chrome policies,

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.670
letting them see what
warnings were circumvented

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:29.270
and what common sites are
attack vectors on your domain.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.830
To keep your passwords
safe, you can

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.080
use Password Alert,
which can notify admins

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.180
when an internal
password has accidentally

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.070
been used for an external site.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.110
This helps fight phishing
and password-sharing

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.280
vulnerabilities.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.410
But security isn't
just a one-way street.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.500
Starting with Chrome
68, non-HTTPS websites

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.630
will be identified
as "not secure,"

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.690
helping us create a web that's
safer from eavesdropping.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:53.870
Even with strong web encryption,
new vectors keep emerging.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:56.990
With Spectre and Meltdown, we
saw machines around the world

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.460
suddenly at risk.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:00.290
We reduced the ability
for malicious code

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:02.330
to spread with sandboxing.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.360
Originally, we built
Chrome with tab sandboxing,

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.120
which prevents tabs from
interfering with each other.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.330
Now with site isolation,
different sites in one tab

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.160
cannot affect each
other or leak data.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.030
Thanks for watching.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.370
You can see a link to the full
talk in the description below.

